# Root-level .dockerignore — applied when a Dockerfile build uses repo root
# as its context (e.g. museum-backend/docker-compose.dev.yml `context: ..`
# so the `file:../packages/musaium-shared` workspace dep can be COPYed
# before `pnpm install`).
#
# Excludes everything outside the backend build surface so the context
# transfer does not balloon (museum-frontend/ios/Pods is ~1 GB of native
# binaries alone).
#
# Per-app .dockerignore files (museum-backend/.dockerignore etc.) remain
# authoritative when those Dockerfiles use a narrower context.

# ─── Heavy / unrelated apps ────────────────────────────────────────────────
museum-frontend
museum-web
design-system
docs
infra
team-reports

# ─── Tool / VCS / agent state ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.github
.husky
.claude
.cursor
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# ─── Per-pkg build artefacts + caches (musaium-shared/dist IS shipped) ─────
**/node_modules
**/coverage
**/.cache
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/dist-server
**/.expo
**/.expo-shared
**/.eas
**/build
**/.test-dist
**/.stryker-tmp
**/.stryker-run

# ─── Env / secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.production.example
!**/.env.host-mode

# ─── Logs / debug ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log
**/yarn-debug.log
**/yarn-error.log

# ─── Python developer artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
# `museum-backend/ops/llm-guard-sidecar/.venv` is 1.0 GB (a virtualenv carrying the
# `transformers` model weights). It is gitignored — but .gitignore has NO effect on
# a Docker build context, and nothing here excluded it, so every `docker build` was
# streaming it in and writing it into an overlay2 layer. That is what filled the
# disk on 2026-07-14 (`failed to solve: ResourceExhausted: … no space left on
# device`, on a rebuild of the *backend* image, which does not use Python at all).
#
# The sidecar does not need it either: its own Dockerfile installs from
# requirements.txt INSIDE the image. The local venv is a developer artifact and
# belongs in no build context.
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# ─── Misc ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/Thumbs.db
